\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1.    O, Lord Jesus, let me love my fellow man.
\par \pard\li315\sl200\slmult0\qj That I place him not under any  judgement
\par That out of hatred I cause him no distress,
\par Nor undermine him.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl200\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   2.  May I uncover his weakness with true  love,
\par \pard\li315\sl200\slmult0 In the face of the shameful acts of the world,
\par \pard\li315\sl200\slmult0\qj Should he thus fall, I his counsel shall be,
\par \pard\li315\sl200\slmult0 And cause him to rise.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   3.   May I well strive to help his welfare  improve,
\par \pard\li315\sl200\slmult0 And make me realize that his life is valued,
\par That thou wast nailed on the cross for  poor sinners,
\par And for him as well.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

